method:
Regex parsing of the video's plain-text description for the literal marker 'Provided to YouTube by <distributor>' followed by a structured block: track title, an 'Artist · Album' style separator line, an optional ℗ copyright year, an optional 'Released on: YYYY-MM-DD' line, and a closing 'Auto-generated by YouTube.' notice. A representative working pattern reported by the developer community: (?s)Provided to YouTube by [^
]+
+(?P<track>[^·]+)·(?P<artist>[^
]+)
+(?P<album>[^
]+)(?:.+?℗\s*(?P<release_year>\d{4})(?!\d))?(?:.+?Released on\s*:\s*(?P<release_date>\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}))?(.+?
Artist\s*:\s*(?P<clean_artist>[^
]+))?, using the middle-dot separator, an optional pressing-year (℗) group, an optional ISO release-date group, and an optional explicit 'Artist:' credit line. [uncertain]
